.TH DOCENGINE 2
.SH NAME
docengine, docreg \- documents for Xenith's document view
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "docengine.m";
include "docreg.m";
docreg := load Docreg Docreg->PATH;

Docreg: module {
	Binary, Source: con iota;
	Kind: adt {
		name:   string;
		class:  int;
		engine: string;
		exts:   list of string;
		magic:  list of array of byte;
	};
	init:    fn(d: ref Draw->Display);
	kind:    fn(name: string, head: array of byte): ref Kind;
	kindof:  fn(name: string): ref Kind;
	engine:  fn(k: ref Kind): (Docengine, string);
	loaded:  fn(): list of string;
	picture: fn(name: string, data: array of byte,
	            s: ref Docengine->Style): (ref Draw->Image, string);
};

Docengine: module {
	Style: adt {
		width:   int;
		font, codefont: ref Draw->Font;
		fg, bg, accent, codebg: ref Draw->Image;
	};
	Run:  adt { text: string; r: Draw->Rect; };
	Link: adt { sheet: int; r: Draw->Rect; url: string; };

	init:      fn(d: ref Draw->Display): string;
	open:      fn(data: array of byte, name: string,
	              s: ref Style): (int, string);
	close:     fn(h: int);
	nsheets:   fn(h: int): int;
	sheetsize: fn(h: int, n: int): Draw->Point;
	restyle:   fn(h: int, s: ref Style): string;
	scalable:  fn(h: int): int;
	paint:     fn(h: int, n: int, scale: int, dst: ref Draw->Image,
	              r: Draw->Rect, org: Draw->Point): string;
	text:      fn(h: int): string;
	sheettext: fn(h: int, n: int): string;
	runs:      fn(h: int, n: int): array of Run;
	links:     fn(h: int): array of Link;
	linkat:    fn(h: int, n: int, p: Draw->Point): string;
	lineto:    fn(h: int, l: int): (int, int);
	lineat:    fn(h: int, n: int, y: int): int;
	commands:  fn(h: int): list of string;
	command:   fn(h: int, cmd, arg: string): string;
	events:    fn(h: int): chan of string;
	name:      fn(h: int): string;
	click:     fn(h: int, n: int, p: Draw->Point): string;
	key:       fn(h: int, r: int): string;
	files:     fn(h: int): string;
};
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
A document is a file shown as it is meant to be seen: a PDF, an image,
a Mermaid diagram, Markdown or HTML set for reading, a web page.
Xenith's window shows every kind with one view; the document itself is
held by an engine, a module that knows one kind.
.PP
.B Docreg
knows the kinds. They are a table,
.BR /lib/xenith/doctypes ,
one kind a line: its name;
.B binary
(always shown as the document, the window's text being the document's
text, read-only) or
.B source
(the window's text is the file's, and Render shows the document); the
engine's module path; the file name extensions, with their dots; and
.BI magic= bytes
the file begins with,
.BI \e x NN
for a byte by its value.
.I Kind
gives the kind of a file by its extension, or failing that by its first
bytes
.IR head ,
or nil if it is to be shown as text.
.I Kindof
gives the kind of a name.
.I Engine
loads a kind's engine the first time it is asked for, initialises it,
and keeps it; reading the table loads nothing.
.I Loaded
lists the engines loaded.
.I Picture
draws a document whole as one image (its first sheet; a flowing
document set to
.IB s .width\f1,
a picture scaled to it), for a program that shows documents as
pictures, such as Lucifer's presentation view.
.PP
An engine holds documents of its kind as sessions named by a handle,
.I h .
Its dependencies (the PDF interpreter, the typesetter, Charon's engine)
it loads when it opens its first document.
.I Open
makes a document from its bytes and its
.I name
(a path or a URL; with
.I data
nil the engine reads the file or fetches the URL), set in
.IR s .
A document is a column of sheets: a PDF's pages, or one sheet for a
picture or for a flowing document laid out to
.IB s .width\f1.
.I Sheetsize
is a sheet's size at scale 100;
.I restyle
sets a flowing document again for a new width or colours.
.I Paint
draws sheet
.I n
at
.I scale
(percent) into the rectangle
.I r
of
.IR dst ,
the point
.I org
of the scaled sheet at
.IB r .min\f1;
an engine for which
.I scalable
is 1 paints sharp at any scale, one for which it is 0 at 100 only, and
the view scales what it paints.
.PP
.I Text
is the document's text: extracted from a binary document, as set from a
source one.
.I Runs
are the words on a sheet as drawn, with their boxes at scale 100, for
hitting a word with the mouse and marking what a search finds; nil if
the engine cannot tell.
.I Links
and
.I linkat
are the document's links.
.I Lineto
and
.I lineat
map a source document's lines to where they are set and back, so a
window keeps its place going from its text to the document.
.I Commands
are the engine's own, beyond the view's (zoom, fit, paging), and
.I command
does one.
.PP
A document that changes by itself or takes the mouse and the keyboard,
a web page, has
.IR events :
a channel giving
.BI done " y
(loaded; its name, text and size may have changed;
.I y
is where its last navigation asks the view to be),
.B update
(laid out again) and
.BI error " msg\f1.
.I Name
is what it shows now.
.I Click
and
.I key
return nil if they were not taken, or what the view is to do:
.B paint
(paint again),
.B layout
(its size changed too) or
.BI show " y0 y1
(bring that part into view).
.I Files
is where the document is served as files, or nil.
.SH FILES
.B /lib/xenith/doctypes
.br
.B /dis/xenith/doc/*.dis
\- the engines: pdfdoc, imgdoc, mddoc, mmddoc, webdoc
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/xenith/docreg.b
.br
.B /appl/xenith/doc/*.b
.br
.B /appl/xenith/docview.b
\- the view
.SH SEE ALSO
.B docs/xenith-documents.md
